ws and columns that share a color, and how they relate to the full diamond shape. I will continue to investigate how other colors map to their respective shapes in the output.\n\n\n**Confirming Shape Boundaries**\n\nI've made a crucial discovery. By meticulously examining the coordinates, specifically rows 4 and 8, I've confirmed the vertical boundaries of the diamond shape. Using the input data, I've realized row 4 and row 8, along with column 3, accurately define the top and bottom points of the diamond, respectively. This gives further proof of the shape's boundaries within the grid.\n\n\n**Verifying Vertex Placement**\n\nI've just made a very important realization! Considering the coordinates for color 5, like at (7, 7) and (11, 7), it seems the input only supplies the top and bottom vertices of the diamond! Furthermore, the input's template disappears in the output and is replaced with zeros! Now, I need to verify that this applies to all the diamonds.\n\n\n",
